@startuml
title Tutor read-only versus writer handoff v1
actor Student
participant "ChatGPT Tutor" as Tutor
participant "Curriculum Reader" as Reader
participant "Assessment Engine" as Assessment
participant "State Validator" as Validator
database "Evidence Store / Git" as Store
Tutor -> Reader : Read current state, catalog and authored lesson
Reader -> Store : Read by commit SHA
Store --> Tutor : Verified checkpoint and pending gaps
Tutor -> Student : Guided task, then independent variant
Student --> Tutor : Output / artifact references
Tutor -> Assessment : Assess evidence within its actual scope
Assessment --> Tutor : Gaps / acceptance proposal
alt Tutor has no write capability
Tutor --> Student : Structured proposal + base SHA; not saved
else authorized writer available
Tutor -> Validator : Check transition, hashes and prerequisites
Validator --> Tutor : Accept or precise errors
Tutor -> Store : Commit only accepted update
Store --> Student : New commit SHA (proof of persistence)
end
note over Tutor,Store
Interrupted session resumes verified checkpoints;
never infer persistence from conversation.
end note
@enduml
